[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2005381020","pull_request_review_id":2702247910,"id":2005381020,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc53h6-c","diff_hunk":"@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ class CommandQueueMT {\n \tuint32_t sync_awaiters = 0;\n \tWorkerThreadPool::TaskID pump_task_id = WorkerThreadPool::INVALID_TASK_ID;\n \tuint64_t flush_read_ptr = 0;\n+\tstd::atomic<bool> pending;","path":"core/templates/command_queue_mt.h","commit_id":"bdb5d522d137e85200738a9f17fc539c4fc2ed96","original_commit_id":"bdb5d522d137e85200738a9f17fc539c4fc2ed96","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We'd rather use `SafeFlag` here. We only use `std::atomic` directly where we need tighter control.\r\n\r\nAside, but even more imporant, note that `std::atomic::store()` and `load()` use total sequential order, which issues much stricter memory barriers, being a potential big pessimization. `SafeFlag` is more relaxed, as it uses acquire-release.","created_at":"2025-03-20T11:21:40Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T11:21:40Z","html_url":"https:/